Darken a shut laptop's panel even with no other monitor

niri turns a laptop's own panel off when its lid shuts only while
another monitor is connected, so a machine kept awake with its lid
shut and nothing plugged in lights a panel nobody can see, and wakes
its touchscreen with it. Shut, the panel goes dark either way, and
opening the lid lights it again; with no output at all, niri runs as
it does when a desktop's only monitor is unplugged.

A lid's switch can be wrong, though: one read shut for two minutes on
a lap, with the lid open, and left nothing lit. So while the lid reads
shut and no screen is lit, a key, a click or a pointer moved, which
nobody can make with the lid shut, takes the lid as open until its
switch next changes. A touch or a pen doesn't, since a shut lid can
press the screen.

